ritage that slavery took away from them, along with their names and their identities. But Roots speaks, finally, not just to blacks, or to whites, but to all people and all races everywhere, for the story it tells is one of the most eloquent testimonials ever written to the indomitability of the human spirit.	4.43	146094	https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/books/1329398936l/546018.jpg
